WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.860
Let me ask you something.

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:03.572
You and I have both worked
at "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:03.572 --> 00:00:04.405
Oh, we're going to--

00:00:04.405 --> 00:00:05.238
And I am curious--
(J.B. laughing)

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.860
'Cause everyone tells me,

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.850
when I was at "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.480
I wasn't one of those quiet writers.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.480
I liked to sort of get up and
perform my ideas for people.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.040
I was the guy that was always talking,

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.270
and I've heard that you were the same way,

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.267
that you liked to, when you had an idea,

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.740
and you wanted to make a comedy pitch,

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.490
that you could make
everybody in the room laugh.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:27.910
Is that true?

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:29.470
Yeah, man, 'cause you know what?

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.590
We had that stand-up mentality.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.510
Now, some people came
in the show, of course,

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.660
as straight writers, and some
came in as stand-up artists.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.860
We are used to being in
front of an audience.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.930
We're used to projecting a certain way,

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:44.520
and we like to paint pictures
of what we're pitching.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:45.830
So that was my style.

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:46.800
You know what I love to hear about is

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.790
I love to hear about the
ideas that never made it

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:50.770
onto "Saturday Night Live."
Whoo hoo!

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:52.190
Those are my favorite ideas.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.161
Do you have any pitches that you did--

00:00:54.161 --> 00:00:54.994
Oh!

00:00:54.994 --> 00:00:57.070
Back in the day that you loved,

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.420
and you got up, and you performed them,

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.080
and it never got on the show?

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:00.913
Oh yeah, man.

00:01:00.913 --> 00:01:01.746
I had a bunch of them, man.

00:01:01.746 --> 00:01:02.579
I had one.

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:03.610
This one I love.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.259
This one I don't understand
why it didn't make it,

00:01:05.259 --> 00:01:06.890
but this is one of my favorite ones.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:10.240
So, I had a guy that
used to work in a bank.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.092
[Conan] Used to work in a bank.

00:01:11.092 --> 00:01:13.510
He was a bank teller for years,
years, doing bank teller.

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:18.510
When you work somewhere, you
start to take on your job.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:20.000
Your job becomes a part of you

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:20.833
'cause you go there every day.

00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:21.800
You're doing it every day.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:22.633
He's a bank teller.

00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:24.527
When you count money, you lick the thumb.

00:01:24.527 --> 00:01:26.670
Lick your thumb, and
you count the money out.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:27.503
[Conan] Right.

00:01:27.503 --> 00:01:28.336
This is a person that's good,

00:01:28.336 --> 00:01:29.716
if you don't have one of those
little round circle sponges

00:01:29.716 --> 00:01:30.737
that you put your thumb in.

00:01:30.737 --> 00:01:31.570
[Conan] Yeah.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:33.217
But anyway, most people are
so used to counting money,

00:01:33.217 --> 00:01:34.228
they lick their thumb--
Yeah, I do that, yeah.

00:01:34.228 --> 00:01:35.108
And they count that money for you,

00:01:35.108 --> 00:01:36.312
lay that money all out for you, right?

00:01:36.312 --> 00:01:41.210
So this guy ends up getting
fired, right, from the bank.

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:42.410
He moved on.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:43.680
He was there for a long time.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.130
He ends up getting a new job.

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:47.000
Now he works at a sandwich shop.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.940
Now, but he's working at a sandwich shop,

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:50.290
like Subway or something like that,

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.210
but he can't get the bank
teller out of his system.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:54.750
So he's making you a sandwich.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:55.583
You want the club sandwich.

00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:58.340
You know the club sandwich
comes with the bacon,

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.930
comes with the turkey, the Swiss.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:02.880
You want that, right?

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.340
And he asks you if you
want Swiss cheese on it,

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.173
and he licks his finger

00:02:06.173 --> 00:02:07.006
(Conan laughing)

00:02:07.006 --> 00:02:09.957
and puts that cheese on it
every time, every single time.

00:02:09.957 --> 00:02:11.068
"You want to add salami?"

00:02:11.068 --> 00:02:12.897
And then, lick the thumb, every time,

00:02:12.897 --> 00:02:14.480
every time he's putting the meat on,

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.356
which is disgusting.

00:02:16.356 --> 00:02:17.280
Uh huh.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:18.113
But he can't stop.
(Conan laughing)

00:02:18.113 --> 00:02:19.910
He can't stop doing it.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:20.870
I love that idea.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:21.780
That didn't get on the air?

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.680
That idea should have made it.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.047
Licking your thumb, making
a sandwich for somebody,

00:02:26.047 --> 00:02:26.880
that should have made it.
Yeah.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.900
That should have made it.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:28.940
What else? You got another one?

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:29.773
I want to hear another one.

00:02:29.773 --> 00:02:30.606
Oh, oh, oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:30.606 --> 00:02:31.826
I got a few of them, man.

00:02:31.826 --> 00:02:32.720
I got one.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:33.830
Oh, oh, oh, oh.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.813
This one right here never made it.

00:02:34.813 --> 00:02:39.220
This was Tom Brady, the
quarterback Tom Brady

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.053
who used to play for the Patriots,

00:02:40.053 --> 00:02:42.350
who now plays for the
Tampa Bay Buccaneers.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.497
This guy, he was a guest on the show.

00:02:43.497 --> 00:02:44.704
[Conan] He was the guest host.

00:02:44.704 --> 00:02:47.400
He was the guest host,
and he came to the show,

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.650
and I wrote this idea for him

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.500
where he was the first player in the NFL

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.140
to smack another man on
the butt after a good play.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.934
Oh, man, but it was a
throwback back to the '40s.

00:02:57.934 --> 00:02:58.767
Yeah.

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:00.912
Back in the days when
guys wore leather helmets.

00:03:00.912 --> 00:03:01.745
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:01.745 --> 00:03:03.010
And he just kept smacking guys on the ass

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:04.830
after a good play, spanking on the ass,

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.730
uhn, spanking on the
ass after a good play.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:09.113
But nobody understood why
this guy was doing this

00:03:09.113 --> 00:03:10.937
for a long time.
(Conan laughing)

00:03:10.937 --> 00:03:12.170
Why does this guy keep doing this?

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:14.570
Why does he keep smacking
people on the butt?

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.700
Nobody understood why he kept doing it,

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.030
so he was the only NFL player in the world

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:21.241
who got traded to every team in the NFL

00:03:21.241 --> 00:03:22.074
(Conan laughing)

00:03:22.074 --> 00:03:24.949
'cause no one understood
what the hell he was doing.

00:03:24.949 --> 00:03:26.507
And when he started
doing it in the shower,

00:03:26.507 --> 00:03:29.712
that's when it went up to another level.

00:03:29.712 --> 00:03:30.597
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:30.597 --> 00:03:31.495
That's a very funny idea.

00:03:31.495 --> 00:03:34.380
I can't believe, I think
that's a good sketch.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.620
Oh, that's a great sketch idea.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:36.453
You kidding me?

00:03:36.453 --> 00:03:38.350
There's a million of them
that should have made it,

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:41.490
and I just don't, but
you know, I digress, man.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.022
It's all good.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:43.855
Well, you don't care.

00:03:43.855 --> 00:03:45.190
They didn't get on the
show, but look at you now.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.900
You're in your zen space.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.390
In my zen space.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:51.753
You're happy.
(J.B. laughing)

